{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"7843905c-5969-4b88-b56f-9b7f00831cc8","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have investigated the issue and fixed the prompt caching behavior.\n\n### Cause of Cache Invalidation\nIn [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-itVJOF/bot.py), `build_system` previously concatenated static coaching instructions (`INSTRUCTIONS`) and dynamic per-athlete state (`athlete_context(a, today)`, which includes the athlete's `facts`) into a single text block with `\"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. Whenever `save_fact` was invoked, `a.facts` was updated. Because caching relies on prefix byte matching across the full block, modifying `athlete_context` invalidated the cache for the entire combined prompt (~1000+ tokens).\n\n### Fix Applied\nUpdated [`build_system`](file:///tmp/h-itVJOF/bot.py#L130-L136) in [`bot.py`](file:///tmp/h-itVJOF/bot.py) to split the system prompt into two separate content blocks:\n1. **Static Block:** Contains `INSTRUCTIONS` with `\"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}` so it stays cached across calls.\n2. **Dynamic Block:** Contains `athlete_context(a, today)` without `cache_control`.\n\nA full summary of the issue, resolution, and mechanism has been written to [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-itVJOF/ANSWER.md).\n","duration_seconds":108.954042,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":160545,"output_tokens":2868,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":568593,"total_tokens":163413}}}
